DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261114T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261114T120000
DTSTAMP:20261110T160933Z
UID:7a73211c21062cbb0bdfcb9a06e751d5@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,educators
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Ticket required\\nAge
 s: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nJoin the Field Museum for Exploring I
 ndigenous Ingenuity in Ancient Americas \, a professional development work
 shop presented in celebration of Native American Heritage Month . Educator
 s will investigate how Indigenous peoples across the Americas developed sc
 ientific knowledge and technological innovations through close observation
 \, experimentation\, creativity\, and relationships with the land. Partici
 pants will engage in inquiry-based\, hands-on activities that explore Indi
 genous ingenuity through a STEAM lens . The workshop will connect ancestra
 l innovations to living Indigenous communities\, contemporary knowledge\, 
 and cultural identity. Open to formal and informal STEAM educators of all 
 grade levels . Illinois educators will earn 3 Professional Development hou
 rs . Registration includes workshop materials and museum admission.\\n\\nM
 ore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/professional-development-
 for-educators/exploring-indigenous-ingenuity-in-ancient-americas
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/professional-development-for-ed
 ucators/exploring-indigenous-ingenuity-in-ancient-americas
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Exploring Indigenous Ingenuity in Ancient Americas
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:In 2 hours: Exploring Indigenous Ingenuity in Ancient Americas
TRIGGER:-PT2H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
