BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[FREE] Celebrate Diwali at the Field Museum!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261115T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261115T170000
DTSTAMP:20261110T160933Z
UID:4c87c14d0539ed9a6231c95d37b436c9@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nJoin us for our second 
 annual Diwali celebration as we honor the Festival of Lights and the rich 
 cultural traditions of South Asia! Experience an afternoon of vibrant danc
 e performances\, interactive cultural activities\, and opportunities to ex
 plore the connections between science\, history\, and tradition. From clas
 sical Indian dance and contemporary Bollywood to an engaging conversation 
 on Ayurveda\, discover how South Asian traditions celebrate light\, knowle
 dge\, and renewal. Music will be provided by DJ J-Mean. Our popular henna 
 station returns this year\, free for all attendees! Guests can also connec
 t with local community organizations and learn more about the diverse cult
 ures\, traditions\, and contributions of South Asian communities throughou
 t Chicagoland. Featured Dance Performances The following take place in Sta
 nley Field Hall Mandala Arts | Bharatanatyam Experience the beauty and sto
 rytelling of Bharatanatyam\, a classical Indian dance tradition rooted in 
 South India. Through intricate movements\, expressive gestures\, and rhyth
 mic footwork\, Mandala Arts brings to life stories and traditions that hav
 e been shared across generations. U Chicago Raas | Raas-Garba Celebrate th
 e energy and joy of Raas-Garba\, traditional folk dances from Gujarat\, In
 dia. U Chicago Raas brings a contemporary collegiate interpretation of the
 se vibrant traditions\, combining rhythmic movement\, colorful choreograph
 y\, and the spirit of community celebration. Latin School of Chicago - Lat
 in Laddoos Performance Group The South Asian Students of the Latin School 
 (Junior K to 8th Grade) will perform contemporary and traditional group da
 nce. They have performed dances choreographed by Bollywood Groove and Mehe
 r Dance in 2026. Rhythm Roots | Bollywood and Indian Folk Dance Get ready 
 for a lively celebration of Indian dance! Featuring talented young perform
 ers ages 6–14\, Rhythm Roots showcases an exciting blend of Bollywood\, 
 Garba\, Bhangra\, and contemporary fusion. Guests will also have an opport
 unity to join the fun through an interactive dance experience!\\n\\nMore i
 nfo: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/celebrate
 -diwali-at-the-field-museum
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/cultural-programming/celebrate-
 diwali-at-the-field-museum
